# nr-relay-frame-policy: wire lines for mixdog-relay (native/core/crates/mixdog-relay): src/legs/envelope.rs and src/legs/policy.rs

Nothing is registered, no protocol method is added and no Cargo line is needed: the crate already depends on `mixdog-js`,
`serde_json` and everything else the two modules use, and `tests/legs_policy.rs` is found by Cargo's own test discovery
(no `[[test]]` entry, no feature).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-relay/src/legs/mod.rs

This task wrote `pub mod envelope;` and `pub mod policy;`. The ingress task (nr-relay-ingress) owns the same file and adds
`pub mod ingress;`: apply both lines when merging.

## What later relay tasks call

`legs::policy`: `send_to_phone` over the `PhoneLeg` trait (the sockets code implements it for a phone leg and owns one
`InflightMeter` per process, one `LegCharge` per socket), `admit_frame`, `uplink_ceilings`, `UplinkLeg`, `relay_capabilities`,
`routed_client_id`, `desktop_oversize_notice`, `phone_oversize_notice`, `check_oversize`, `desktop_gone_notice_due`, and the constants.
`legs::envelope`: `encode_frame`, `decode_frame`, `json_frame`, `is_transport_frame`, `is_phone_ping`, `PHONE_PONG`.
